# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# The security policy the app assumes lives HERE, not in a <meta> tag. The long
# comment at the top of index.html explains why: a meta CSP applies to whatever
# loads that file, and `flutter run -d chrome` calls main() from an inline
# script that `script-src 'self'` refuses - so the debug app hangs on the splash
# screen with no Dart error and a clean build log. Headers also express what a
# meta tag never can: frame-ancestors is ignored in meta by every browser, so
# clickjacking protection is a header or it does not exist.
#
# Everything in web/ is copied verbatim into build/web/, which is what deploys -
# the same mechanism that ships _redirects and the legal pages.
#
# Three entries in connect-src are easy to leave out, and all three fail
# quietly:
#
#   - the Sentry ingest host. Crash reports are a POST governed by connect-src.
#     Omit it and every report is blocked in the browser, the dashboard stays
#     empty, and the only evidence is a console line nobody reads in production.
#     It must match the host in SENTRY_DSN.
#
#   - www.gstatic.com in connect-src, not only script-src. Flutter's default web
#     renderer downloads CanvasKit from gstatic; the loader is a <script>, but
#     the .wasm beside it is a fetch. Building with --no-web-resources-cdn
#     self-hosts CanvasKit and lets both gstatic entries go - worth doing, since
#     the privacy policy promises no third parties.
#
#   - blob: in connect-src, not only in img-src and worker-src. Picking a photo
#     on web hands back an XFile whose path is a blob: URL, and the
#     readAsBytes() every picker call site uses reads it with an XHR - a fetch,
#     so connect-src governs it, not img-src. Without it product images and
#     payment proofs cannot be uploaded at all on web, and the only symptom is
#     a CSP line in the console. blob: URLs are minted by this origin and
#     cannot address anything remote, so allowing the scheme exfiltrates
#     nothing.
#
# The Supabase origin is per-environment, which is the other reason this is not
# baked into the bundle. Update both supabase.co entries when the project ref
# changes.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://www.gstatic.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://qnacxjlbmdopwvikkocq.supabase.co; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' blob: https://qnacxjlbmdopwvikkocq.supabase.co wss://qnacxjlbmdopwvikkocq.supabase.co https://o4511879257915392.ingest.de.sentry.io https://www.gstatic.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(self), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), interest-cohort=()

# style-src keeps 'unsafe-inline' for one reason: the cold-start splash <style>
# in index.html has to paint before any extra request could return. The
# splash-removal *script* was moved to splash.js precisely so that script-src
# needs no such exception - do not undo that by inlining it again.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Caching.
#
# Flutter does not content-hash its top-level JavaScript. main.dart.js keeps its
# name across builds and versioning is done inside flutter_service_worker.js, so
# a long max-age on any of these pins a shop to whatever build it first loaded -
# a bug that reproduces for exactly the users you cannot reach.
#
# Only the two directories whose contents are addressed by hash or version are
# safe to freeze.

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/flutter_bootstrap.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/flutter_service_worker.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/main.dart.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/version.json
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/manifest.json
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/canvaskit/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
